WEBVTT

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.010
Shit...

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.090
That bastard used me as a meat shield.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.800
A penniless, powerless, novice Jushikiist...

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.290
I get used up, and that's it.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.850
This is bullshit.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.940
This is bullshit.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.800
Such a pathetic victory is a 
humiliation to the Draken people.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.310
It certainly hurt that we 
lost one of the rearguard.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:44.680
If only there were a good 
Jushikiist just lying around.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.830
They wouldn't be lying around if 
they were any good, Chief Diorg.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.780
Let's just up and die now.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.730
Hey, now, Stratos, we wouldn't 
want to lose even more men.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.460
Too bad.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.440
I'll think of another way to die, then.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.470
Diorg...

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:05.580
I found some trash for you.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.000
Over there.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.460
But he looks to be dead already.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.510
Who are you calling trash, you peabrain?

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:25.590
<i>This happened back when I had 
slightly higher aspirations.</i>

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:03.030
<b>And Yet, We...</b>

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.540
I did it.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:09.540
Fool!

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.040
A rearguard who gets the front line hurt 
is even more dangerous than an enemy.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.650
We aren't amateurs here!

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:21.140
You're just too slow to dodge, you slowpoke!

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.050
All right, then.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.430
I have no use for an incapable rearguard!

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.440
Cuello...

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:42.240
I assume you don't value your life, 
if you're standing in front of a Draken's sword.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.350
I value my life.

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:48.090
But I won't allow pointless 
killing on my watch.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:48.990
Never!

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:53.370
Removing useless trash isn't pointless.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.400
That decision is up to Chief Diorg.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.880
As the chief isn't here,

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.630
you'll be taking orders 
from the deputy chief—me.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.140
You really are an annoying woman.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:09.620
I'll take that as a compliment.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.560
Hey, where are you going?

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.770
To the furniture shop.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.150
Don't talk to me for a while.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:17.820
Jeez.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.470
You were the one who picked him up.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.400
I don't care if he's a Draken or whatever.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.920
Warfare freaks like him ought to 
play with their toys in hell.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:31.460
Take a good look at what you've done.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:39.480
This is the result of your 
foolishness and arrogance.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.170
I hate Gigina.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.720
I'm fundamentally incompatible with him.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.810
Then you ought to make yourself compatible.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.000
Same goes for that attack earlier.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.040
You shouldn't have tried 
to fight on your own.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:06.660
You should have relied on Gigina's assistance
 or waited for my lightning Jushiki.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.830
You used a needlessly, excessively huge Jushiki

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.770
just to show off your skills.

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:16.790
Are you listening to me?

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:18.660
Sorry.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.800
I do nothing but cause you grief 
because of my inexperience.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:25.820
It's not really grief.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.340
I was anxious.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.210
I couldn't keep dragging 
everyone down forever.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:34.890
If I don't make myself useful, 
I'll be abandoned again.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.560
We don't abandon our own.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:41.570
Cuello, please don't hate me.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:43.420
I don't hate you.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:44.520
Then...

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.450
I've always wanted...

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.810
to do this.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:00.590
<i>To take advantage of a 
righteous bitch like you</i>

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:04.540
<i>and then throw her out like scrap paper.</i>

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.590
What do you think you're doing?

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.220
Do you happen to hate men?

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.810
I like men.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:17.070
They make good Jushikiists.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:21.150
Especially if they're real men 
who won't try to act pathetic

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.130
just to win a woman's pity.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:27.490
I'd never sleep with you.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.130
The feeling is mutual.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:34.200
I have no interest in men who 
are cowardly and weaker than me.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:41.650
Yes?

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:42.540
Yes.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:43.500
Okay.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.060
Understood.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.470
What do I do?

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:50.480
Stratos and the chief are out on business.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:52.640
And with Gigina's acting the way he is...

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.840
What about me?

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.940
What a cheap act.

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:00.110
At least you get back on your feet quickly.

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:03.030
So, do you have the guts to come with me?

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:09.650
Our target today is Maslow Gossum.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.260
He's good-looking.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.660
Marriage fraud or something?

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:18.190
A month ago, he attacked a jewelry store 
and killed two security Jushikiists.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.170
He made off with a hundred million 
yen's worth of merchandise.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:24.860
He was later arrested by Largonkin's men,

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:27.670
but he escaped while 
out on bail awaiting his trial.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:30.940
All before he revealed 
the whereabouts of the stolen goods.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.180
He got bail after committing
murder and robbery?

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:34.920
Yeah.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.920
And to come up with that bail,

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:41.470
he's borrowed an incredible amount 
of money from a bail bond agent.

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:45.560
But if you flee, 
the court gets to keep the money.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.190
Does he hope to screw them over?

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:50.090
That's why we were hired.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.160
Our client, the bond agent,

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.410
requested that we capture Maslow before 
the police do, during his bail period.

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.200
Of course, no killing him.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.880
The problem, though...

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.680
Claymore...

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:04.960
He's a chemical manipulation Jushikiist?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.800
He's skilled, too. A 10th-rank.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:09.800
Want out?

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.180
N-No way.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:13.470
So what's the plan?

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.470
First, we'll go through his past 
and figure out where he's hiding.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.970
We don't make a scene until then.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:29.050
One request and you sell out one of your own.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:30.730
What a time to be alive.

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:34.860
Sadly, humans are ungrateful creatures.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:39.550
Well, that's how we managed 
to find him, though.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:40.980
I guess it's all good.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:45.370
Now we just have to catch him or kill him.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.380
I said no killing.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:51.620
More of your righteous talk?

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:54.880
Killing is part of the business.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:58.950
I'll go in first and neutralize him.

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:02.020
You're only to serve as my backup.

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.890
I know.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:07.150
Pardon me.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.400
We're from the power company.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:11.420
We're here for an inspection.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:12.660
Is anyone home?

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.070
He got away!

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:22.410
Die!

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.830
Shit!

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:36.740
Stop!

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:42.570
Shit.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.110
Gayus!

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:49.300
Gayus!

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:53.190
Hang in there, Gayus.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:58.720
Sorry... I caused you more trouble.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.240
Save your self-loathing 
and reflection for later.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:05.820
<i>Huh? Am I...</i>

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.400
Stay conscious.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.700
<i>...going to die?</i>

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:09.770
Gayus!

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.370
Oh jeez, you're awake?

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:54.120
You didn't do anything to me 
while I was asleep, did you?

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:56.340
Obviously not!

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:00.020
Why did you save me?

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:04.250
I ignored your orders.

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:07.140
If I'd died, it would've been my own fault.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:11.190
You didn't have a reason to put 
yourself in danger just to save me.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:15.500
Between a 6th-rank like me 
and 11th-rank like you...

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:18.200
Our lives don't have the same worth.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:27.040
Gayus, you must have been fighting
in a really awful way until now.

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:30.580
It's normal to put your own life 
on the line for the people on your team.

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:34.840
That's our policy at Diorg Jushikiist Agency,

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:36.920
and my own personal belief.

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:41.500
You need to learn to believe in 
and depend on people a little, newbie.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:45.120
You don't need to be ashamed.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:49.120
I was dragging everyone down at first, too.

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:51.840
I've gotten ahead of myself and screwed up.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:54.440
I've cried at how powerless I was.

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.620
Right now's the time to learn.

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:02.010
As long as you make yourself more 
useful over time, it's all right.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:04.640
Cuello...

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:05.700
Yes?

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:08.980
Thanks.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:14.250
Well, you can't stay in bed forever.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.300
I had the chief call Gigina in.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:20.590
We're headed for a rematch 
as soon as we meet up.

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:23.420
I've already set up our information warfare.

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:25.470
You're strong.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.060
I'm not strong.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:31.850
It still scares me that my enemies 
and I are trying to kill each other.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:35.600
But more than my own fear,

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:40.180
my hatred for those who 
hurt others galvanizes me.

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:45.590
I want to do what I can 
to protect the people I love.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:50.240
I don't want to kill my enemies 
if I can help it, either.

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:53.700
It may sound like self-righteous hypocrisy,

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:59.370
but even if I get laughed at, 
even if I'm mocked for it,

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:02.980
I'll never waver in my belief.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:06.460
Cuello...

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:09.140
The way I feel about you right now...

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:17.650
The way he's ringing the bell, 
that must be Gigina.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.560
Oh.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:24.030
You're alive.

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:25.820
You four-eyed loser.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:31.660
Die, dim-witted pigs!

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:32.750
Speed!

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:34.660
Everything is about speed!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.540
I'm the queen of speed!

00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:39.200
Gigina!

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:41.950
Why didn't you stop her 
before she started driving?

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:44.860
Cuello, calm down, please!

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:44.860
Out of the way!

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:50.120
Here comes the massacre demon
 of the mountain path!

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:56.010
So, what's the strategy now?

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:57.760
How do we find Maslow?

00:13:57.760 --> 00:13:59.370
It's simple.

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:02.960
Maslow is likely on edge 
after the incident yesterday.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:07.390
Even if he isn't, high-dollar gems 
are hard to sell in this nation.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:10.570
In either case, the most
 certain course of action...

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:12.660
Is to leave the country.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:19.110
But for a wanted man like Maslow 
to get through border security,

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:21.220
he would need a fake passport.

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:23.210
Correct.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:26.440
Remember how I said I'd set up
 our information warfare?

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.540
Lay down the bait,

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:32.180
and they'll come to get caught themselves.

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:38.410
Where are you?

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:41.020
I'm here with the passport money.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:47.740
You should have paid the 
forger some hush money.

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:53.240
I doubt you'll get anywhere by resisting.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.140
Who do you think I am?!

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:19.690
Gayus!

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:28.310
You're weak.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.320
Go to hell, you four-eyed scrub!

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:35.240
Are you trying to kill me, asshole?!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:35.800
Look out!

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:12.340
Well then, now we just tie him up, and...

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:14.410
Gigina?

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:17.240
Wait, Gigina!

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:25.170
Haven't I told you that if you stand in 
front of a Draken sword, you're dead?

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:28.670
I'll kill any enemy who 
forces me to spill blood.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:32.240
There's something I can't give up, either.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:33.790
I'll tell you again.

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:36.930
I won't let you kill anyone.

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:40.930
Your beliefs are nothing but pretty words.

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:44.910
Still, I have my pride.

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:46.690
Just as you do.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:50.190
If this isn't enough blood for you...

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:51.210
Don't bother.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:53.700
I don't have a need for your blood.

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:07.130
Cuello, give me your arm.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:17.220
That's impressive.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:20.440
Gigina's a master of healing Jushiki.

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:22.010
I'm fine now.

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:22.940
Thanks.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:28.620
Your strength and intensity are 
worthy of a certain kind of praise.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.700
I'd like to fight you to the death someday.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:37.110
I'm just doing everything I can.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:41.640
I'll never become a heartless executioner.

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:48.400
All right, everyone, get together.

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:50.520
We're taking a picture

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:54.490
to commemorate a successful mission 
and the addition of a new member to our team.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:58.760
Wh-Why is the chief all beat up?

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:01.150
Wasn't he out for a meeting?

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:05.770
Apparently, he got caught in an 
attempted suicide bombing by Stratos.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:08.120
I almost had it.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:11.610
Hurry up and take the picture, damn it.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:16.280
A little more to the left, Gigina.

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:19.820
And raise your head a little, Stratos.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:20.810
Okay!

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:22.230
Now, smile!

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.290
Come on, look forward and smile.

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:32.790
From now on, depend on us, 
and let us depend on you.

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:38.620
All right. Here we go.

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:51.450
You definitely need a shelf.

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:53.980
Did you say something?

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:57.890
You need a shelf to organize all of that.

00:18:57.890 --> 00:18:58.860
I know.

00:18:58.860 --> 00:18:59.990
I'll make you one.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:05.490
If you call that giant piece of trash
 you made a "shelf," no thanks.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:10.000
Are you mocking my beloved son Tarelk?!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.590
Yeah. Trash gives birth to trash.

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:13.580
Now, help me out a little!

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:15.980
How dare you, you toxic waste?!

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:20.840
Let's not do this today.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.140
This is never going to get finished.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:29.370
It's not getting finished because you 
waste time reminiscing in silly memories.

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:35.140
It seems Remedius died.

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:37.780
I know.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.030
I see.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:45.780
<i>After Dochetta's death, 
Urmun entered into a nasty civil war.</i>

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:50.440
<i>The Dragon Empire deployed the military
 in the name of peacekeeping.</i>

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:55.240
<i>But I doubt that man will 
do any more than that.</i>

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:59.640
<i>So long as Urmun continues 
to churn in political turmoil,</i>

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:02.900
<i>the Dragon Empire's economy stays stable.</i>

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:05.900
<i>It's as rational a conclusion 
as you could reach.</i>

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:09.310
<i>In the end, most of the people of Urmun</i>

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:12.460
<i>never responded to the Aurora Hammer's call.</i>

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:16.570
<i>After sporadic regional 
revolts and resistances,</i>

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:22.220
<i>they, too, fell apart, and Remedius died...</i>

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:26.070
<i>As the Man-Eating Dragon of the Sand, Zhuo Lu.</i>

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:29.980
<i>His corpse, as it was found 
outside of the city, was decapitated.</i>

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:32.440
<i>It's believed he was assassinated.</i>

00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:37.160
Gayus, are you there?

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:41.660
Come on, hurry up.

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:42.340
Where are we going?

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.260
To the seabird shop.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:49.260
I had us invited to Largonkin's 
welcome home party.

00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:53.130
Jabeira and Iegie are coming, too.

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:56.100
Wait, does that mean we're...

00:20:56.470 --> 00:21:00.360
Do you never learn?

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.960
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:04.270
Never mind that...

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:05.280
Crab!

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.480
We're going to have crab!

00:21:07.480 --> 00:21:08.540
What the hell?

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:09.800
Unhand me, woman.

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:11.120
I'll do no such thing.

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:14.060
<i>The golden age has passed.</i>

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:18.950
<i>The sky I saw then will never return.</i>

00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:20.490
<i>Still...</i>

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:22.970
Hurry, hurry!

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:27.240
I'm never saying what I did again. Ever.

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:27.240
<i>I have a woman I love,</i>

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:29.640
<i>and a partner who has my back.</i>

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:36.980
<i>Beneath this sky is the world 
I both loathe and love.</i>

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:38.900
<i>In which case...</i>

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.980
Gayus!

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:47.910
Hurry up already!

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:53.340
Yeah, I'm coming.

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:56.010
<i>I have all I need.</i>

00:21:56.010 --> 00:21:57.060
<i>Don't I?</i>
